# Interstitium Labs — edge redirects.
# Served two ways:
#   1. This _redirects file (edge, Workers Static Assets).
#   2. docs/worker.js code-level 301s as the backstop: /os and /proof have no
#      asset files, so those requests miss the asset bundle and reach the worker.
# Deploy notes (2026-10-04):
#   - The API deploy passes explicit bindings, which replaces the auto-injected
#     assets binding — the deploy config must also include
#     {"type":"assets","name":"ASSETS"} or env.ASSETS is undefined in worker.js.
#   - run_worker_first must stay UNSET: when set, the worker serves every
#     request via env.ASSETS and the _headers file is silently bypassed
#     (no CSP, no HSTS, no X-Robots-Tag). Default assets-first keeps _headers.
/os       /learn/     301
/os/      /learn/     301
/proof    /evidence/  301
/proof/   /evidence/  301
